From: Dominik Weber <doweb85@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:30:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/27] byteplan: keep the system+tools checkpoint, prewarm it
 from the web UI

- server: neither checkpoint eviction rule drops the checkpoint at the first user message
  (end of system prompt + tool definitions, shared by every new chat)
- web UI: after the server is ready, send the shared start (system message from the
  settings, enabled tools as the agentic flow sends them, empty user message, max_tokens 1)
  once, so the first message of a new chat reuses it
Measured (agent tools, 1.7k tokens): new chat 4.4 s -> 0.14 s processing, after a long chat
4.6 s -> 0.15 s; outputs unchanged.
